  "content_description": "",
  "content_text_body": "Front-line employees are the closest to customers. Produce high quality products and services by listening to and acting on ideas from the front lines. The goal is to be fully present when listening so that you can evaluate and implement ideas that can improve the quality of products and services.\n\n ### Listening tips for leaders\n\n Acknowledging your team members' unique experiences and consider their individual points of view. Be sure to take the time to think carefully about how suggestions, perspectives, or ideas can improve products or services, even if only in small ways.\n\n Practice these [Listening Tips](Glint_Leadership_Tips_for_Being_a_Better_Listener) to become a better listener and leader.\n\n ### Act on good ideas\n\n When team members come to you with good ideas, encourage them to think critically about those ideas to evaluate their potential. Help them brainstorm ways to implement these ideas at your company, encouraging them to take the lead.",
